        <p>WIDOW WHLCH'S PILLS FOR FRMALB COMPLAINTS MRS. SMITHERS Grand-daughter to the Widow Welch, continues to prepare this celebrated Medicine from the only original and genuine Family Recipe. Its just celebrity for all Female Complaints has obtained for it a most extensive and increasing demand Purchasers should therefore attend to the following CAUTION,—To be careful that what they purchase is prepared by Mrs. Smithers, who is the only person in possession of the ORIOINIL RECITE. The genuine are wrapped in Blue Paper, and signed on the OutPide I Abol by Mrs. Smithers, and the names of the Sole Wholesale Agents," W. EDWARDS as SoN 157, Queen Victoria-street," formerly of 67, St. Pau Is' London, are engraved on the Government Stamp, Bold In boxes at 2s. 9d. each by most Chemist.</p>
        <p>NOTICE: NEW 'BUS SERVICE. AR MEE'S ARMS, FEARNHEAD. JOSEPH ROBERTS BEGS to ANNOUNCE that the 'BUSSES running from Central Station to Fearnhead, pass close to the Farmers' Arms. GOOD BOWLING GREEN, SPLENDID ACCOMMODATION FOR CYCLISTS. Dinners, Teas, etc., provided at any time at reasonable charges. Visitors are entertained by Request with Edison's latest Phonograph—a treat. GREENALL'S CELEBRATED ALES, and Stout. Wines, Spirits, and cigars of the Best Quality. A FIRST-CLASS PHOTOGRAPHIC STUDIO, ATTENDED TO BY A HIGHLY QUALIFIED ARTIST. Every Class of Photographic Work finished in the Best and Most Recent Style. WEDDING AND OTHER GROUPS A SPECIALITIE. EDDES DANDELION COFFEE</p>
        <p>- The best and cheapest ever offered to the Public. Sold by all Grocers and Druggists, in Canister sd„ 10d., and Is. Bd. each. Wholesa:e by J. GEDDES Awn SON. WARRINGTON HSTABLIHED 1833</p>
        <p>THE BELFAST HOUSE. JOHN WILSON &amp; SON, (BELFAST) LIMITED DEG to inform their former patrons and the Pub- l.) lie generally that they are showing in their NEW BRANCH WAREHOUSE 761 BOLD STREET, LIVERPOOL a large Assortment of their celebrated HAND WOVEN DAMASK TABLE CLOTHS, NAPKINS, SHEETINGS, PILLOW LINENS, TOWELLING, CAMBRIC POCKET HAND. KERCHIEFS, ALSO GENTLEMENS' SHIRTS, COLLARS &amp; CUFFS AND LADIES' AND CHILDEENS' UNDBRCLOTHINQ of their own manufacture all of which they will SELL at BONA-FIDE MANUFACTURERS' PRICES ALL ARE INVITED to CALL and INSPECT, no one importuned to BUY. LADIES' TROUSSEAU A SPECIALITY. JOHN WILSON &amp; SON, (BELFAST), LTD 76, BOLD STREET, LIVERPOOL. DOWNSHIRE HOUSE, BELFAST. 105, HOPE STREET, GLASGOW. 63, NEW STREET, BIRMINGtiAIII, HARR/MI.IF FACTORY. BALLYMERE.</p>
        <p>SPECIAL ATTENTION PAID TO NEATNESS AND</p>
        <p>Elegance in PROSPECTUSES, PROGRAMMES, itc. PROGRAMMES FOR BAZAARS. PROGRAMMES FOR SALES OF WORK. PROGRAMMES FOR SOIREES. PROGRAMMES FOR CONCERTS. PROGRAMMES FOR FETES, &amp;c. Auctioneers' Sale Bills. Catalogues, Conditions of Sale. Circulars, Pamphlets, Price Lists, Programmes for Concerts. Soirees, Bails, zte. ; Rules for Friendly, Building, and Co-operative Societies ; Cricket Club Rules, Time Sheets and Books,Note Hatttiings,Memorandums,Work Notes,Bill Heads, Easiness Visiting and Mourning CArds, Handbills, Ac. ' Solicitors, Merchinte, Manufact,urers,Tradesmen, and others Lrequiring Printing of any description are requested to give a I trial.</p>
        <p>ALL ORDERS EXECUTED PUNCTUALLY, CORRECTLY, AND ECONOMICALLY</p>
