        <head>WARRINGTON TOWN COUNCIL. THE MAYOR THANKED.</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON TOWN COUNCIL. THE MAYOR THANKED.</p>
        <p>The monthly meeting of this Council was e 1 in thl Council Chamber at the Town Hall. W.,..‘,ir,!t?n, on Tuesday evening. The Mayor (Alderman o sided, and there were alsl pressrat. A; 1,-,rman Fair- clougri (deputy mayor), Alderman R]berts, AldPrnrin Sutton. Alderman Francomb,Alderman Elarrson ; Coun- cillors Shaw Green, Smethurit, Longtou, Berm, E li- sn. John Evans, James Evans, Duncan, Baird, nunion, Peacoclse, Jolley, Rogers, Slaillcoek, Joan Reberta. F. R. Roberts, Burton, Lae, Longtoo,with tr. J Lyon WhiWe (town clerk), Mr. Stanley Wilson (deputy town clerk), Mr. Longdiu (borough surveyor).Mr. Fairhurit (oorough treasurer), Dr. Gornall (medical officer), Mr. Deli (eacii- tary engineer), Mr. Haddock (gas engineer). Tile minuttm of a number of committees, which con- tained little of publics interest were adopted without dis- cuision.</p>
