        <p>This week we are able to give the result of the competition arranged amongst the winners of the Consolation Prize in the No. 7 Football Competition. The £2 Prize has been won by _ _ _</p>
        <p>Mr. H W Gap, 6, Vale Terrace. Dudbridge, near Stroud, THREE WARRINGTON WINNERS.</p>
        <p>The following competitors have been awarded the 20 half; sovereigns: Mr J Hastry, 6 Bfackharst-street, Warrington Mr F Boyle, 11 Atherstene-street, Warrington; Mr 14 Oliffe, Wash-lane, Latchford; Mr J H Martin. 7 Culcross-road, South Tottenham, London: Mr J 14 Lewis, 32 Gopsall-street, Leilester : Mr C Miller, Spilsby, Lincolnshire ; Mr F Johns, 34 Gifford-terrace. Musley, Plymouth ; Mr S F Cocking, 41 Kent-street, Moricetown, Devonpart ; Mr A Martin, 8 Daniel-place, Penzance.; Mr S Harris. 31 High-street. Galley Hill, Swanscombe, Kent; Mr P Anderson, Long Buckby, Northants; Mr G Willington, 24 Mary-street. Old Tiver- ton-road, Exeter: Mr W Marshall, 8 North-street, Exeter; Mr H Cooke. Ruscombe, Near Stroud, Glos. ; Mr D Thompson, Kew-road, Richmond ; Mr P HEnderson, Villiers Hotel, Dough's, I. of M. ; Mr H B Olney, 21 Market Place St. Albans, Herts. ; Mr R Danby, Kingstborpe, near Northampton ; Mr C Gregory, 84 Hope-street. Jarrow-on- Tyne. One COUDOII no name or address. There were two mistakes on th coupon without name ar address. The sender must forward tfl exact copy of the coupon with his claim.</p>
        <p>krizes to the total value of £l2 will be forwarded to the above-named winners on Saturday, November 11th.</p>
