      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-11-03_WidnesExaminer_art0088" n="art0088">
        <head>Daresbury Petty Sessions.</head>
        <p>Daresbury Petty Sessions.</p>
        <p>TUESDkY.—Bef or a Nteisr+. W Long (in the chair). H. Field H. Talbot and Colonel Ridgway. . _ _</p>
        <p>LICSNSING.—NIr. Browne appll,l, on -beh-alf of Mr. J. T. Blwards for the transfer of a wine and spirit license at a shop at Stockton "(Path from Mr. J. 11. Herders, and the application was granted.—Mr. Arthur de Prez applied for a three mouths' Scenic to sell at the Church Institute, Granted.—Mr. C. Rowe was granted permission to sell at a farm sale at Whitley on the 14th Novenvuor. THRICE MONTHS ma THEFT —James Barker, a tramp, was charged with stealing from Ellen Hatch, a music case and three b3oks of music, valued at es ed. From the evidence it appears that the prisoner went up to the proseoutrix and took the case containing the music from her, saying that he wished to feel inside it. Re was detained by two cyclists and was arrested by P.C. Buxton, The prisoner denied the charge, but he was committed to prison for three months' with hard labour.</p>
        <p>A JUVENILE THIRP—John Tulberry (aged 13), of Warring- ton, was charged with st,allog a basket, a bottle of wincand lib of fish. value 31., from a *art at Stockton Heath on the 30th October, the property of Jane Lawson. The evidence showed that the horse and trap belonging to the provecutria were standing outside the Mulberry Tree Inn, Stockton Heath, when the prisoner took the articles out and oarri-d theta away, except the bottle, whioh he dropped and broke. The prisoner was arrested at Messrs. Dutton's shop. War- rington. He gave no reason for taking the things, and he was bound over to come up for judgment when required. Simon Ornexces. —The following were fined for various offences —Drulk and disorderly. ii-nry Shaw. :Os ; drunk In charge. Peter Simpson, 5s and costs; asleep in charge. William Hunt, 55 ; no light, Thomas Whitehead, carter 2s 6d; no light. George Williams, 6. Crosaeld-street. Warrington 5s Arthur Price and James nustlege, of Stockton Heath, were each fined Is for letting off fireworks at Stockton Heath on the 7th October ; Elizabeth Cook. of Hill Cliff, summoned for; assaulting Lily Lyons on the 16th October, was bound over to k eep the peace for six months.</p>
      </div>
