        <p>Playing at hmne, Batley provt-d too strong for C3stlt, ford, deteating them by oue peaaity goal and one try to nil. Davies was again in turn, kicking the goat and ob taming the try.</p>
        <p>LANCASHIRE JUNIOR LEAGUE.</p>
        <p>Widnes Rangers v. Warrington St. Mary's.</p>
        <p>N, mei -liggiaboLtom kicked off, a scrimmage resulting. 'f is.n the Ranger+ pressei, and tbe ball went dead. St. Mary's kicked off, and the Ran-ors pressed, Varley scoring, but the Rams player failed at goal. The Rangers pressel, and eventually Jones scored. Varley kicked .a goal. Afterwards Jones kicked a penalty goal. Ralf-time :—Rangers, two goals, two tries; Warrington Sr. Mary's, nil. In the senind half Speed sclred a try. Varley kicking tbe goal. Final :—Rangers, three goals three tries ; Warrington St Mary's. nil.</p>
