        <head>WARRINGTON RESERVISTS.</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON RESERVISTS.</p>
        <p>Help for the Families. At a meeting of the General Purposes Committee, held at the Town Hall, Warrington a number of gentlemen were appointed a committee to form a fund (1) for the relief of the wives and children of reservists while serving with the Colours, (2) the Refugees from the Tranwtaal, (3) the widows, orphans and other dependents of soldiers who may lose their lives in the war. The committee is composed of the Mayor, Alderman Roberts, Mr. Monks, Colonel Ridgwey, Captan Rdelsten, and Captain H.utchinson. Tbe Mayor on bAalf of the committee lies issued an appeal to the inhabitants of Warrington and the neighbourhood for their co-operation and assist- ance. It is felt, the circular states, that the needs of the wives and families of the reserves recalled to the colours from Werrington and the neighbour- hood demand prompt considereion, and the sub- scriptions received will be devoted to their relief unless subscribers desire their contributions to be otherwise applied. The .absence of tt.e reserves from their wives and families may be prolonged to six months. Subscriptions for. the relief of the Transvaal refugees. and ?f widows, orphans and other dependents of soldiers who may lose their lives in the war, will be transmitted to the Lord Mayor of L-mdon as part of the Mansion House fund. The War Office have promised to farm. h the names and addresses of those Reservists who hti,ve been recalled to the Colours from Warrington and the neighbourhood, and a statement will he issued as soon as tApjinformetien is received of tie help re- quired tollefrieud their wives and families. Sub-</p>
